{"id":"eda7b80fc497e994c35cbbf8214ffccbbf543fb4","individual_note":false,"notes":[{"id":45570,"type":"DiscussionNote","body":"**🟡 Best Practice: PopScope canPop set to false prevents all back navigation**

**File:** `lib/view/features/auth/new_password/new_password_screen.dart`

The success bottom sheet uses 'PopScope(canPop: false)' which completely prevents the back button from working. This might trap users in the bottom sheet if there's an issue with the navigation logic in onPopInvokedWithResult. Consider allowing back navigation but handling it appropriately.

**Current Code:**
```dart
PopScope(
  canPop: false,
  onPopInvokedWithResult: (didPop, result) {
    if (!didPop) {
      Get.back(closeOverlays: true);
      _globalProfileController.navigateToLoginPage();
    }
  },
  child: PlatinumInformationBottomSheet(...),
)
```

**Suggested Fix:**
```dart
PopScope(
  canPop: true,
  onPopInvokedWithResult: (didPop, result) {
    if (didPop) {
      // Bottom sheet was dismissed
      Get.offAllNamed(AppRoute.login);
    }
  },
  child: WillPopScope(
    onWillPop: () async {
      Get.offAllNamed(AppRoute.login);
      return false;
    },
    child: PlatinumInformationBottomSheet(...),
  ),
)
```

**Recommendation:** Allow back navigation (canPop: true) but ensure the navigation to login page happens regardless. Use Get.offAllNamed instead of navigateToLoginPage to ensure all previous routes are cleared and the user can't navigate back to the password setup screen.

---
